Rate: $3/h (If you want more, don't apply, your proposal will be automatically rejected).

I am after asp.net developer who has very good experience with TikTok API.

The first project is to use TikTok Sandbox app to get login working and get video stats, future iteration will expand on that and also will need submitting for production app;

We are looking for a Senior Fullstack Engineer & Team Lead with expertise in .NET and React 18, requiring a minimum commitment of 40 hours per week for 2 years, to drive the development of scalable, high-performance web applications.

This role requires a strong technical leader who can guide a development team, ensuring best practices in software architecture, Agile methodologies, and team collaboration. You will be responsible for leading technical discussions, mentoring engineers, and driving the development of end-to-end solutions, from backend APIs to modern, responsive frontend applications.

Requirements:

- at least 7+ years of experience in fullstack development, with expertise in .NET (C#) and React;
- strong proficiency in React, TypeScript, state management (Redux, MobX, or similar), and component-based architecture;
- expertise in RESTful API development, microservices, and cloud-based architectures;
- experience working with SQL and NoSQL databases (PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB);
- hands-on experience with CI/CD pipelines, Docker, Kubernetes, and cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP);
- experience in leading engineering teams, mentoring developers, and driving Agile best practices;
- strong problem-solving and analytical skills, with the ability to architect scalable and maintainable solutions.
- excellent communication skills and ability to work in fast-paced, collaborative environments.

Nice to Have:
- experience with GraphQL and gRPC.
- knowledge of unit testing (Jest, xUnit, NUnit), integration testing, and test automation.
- familiarity with performance optimization techniques for both frontend and backend applications.
- experience in technical hiring and team scaling.

Key Responsibilities:
- to lead a team of engineers, providing technical direction, mentorship, and hands-on support;
- to develop and optimize backend services using C#, .NET Core, and .NET 6+;
- to design and build modern, scalable frontend applications using React;
- to architect and implement microservices-based solutions, ensuring scalability and maintainability;
- to collaborate with product managers, designers, and DevOps teams to deliver high-quality software;
- to optimize SQL and NoSQL databases (PostgreSQL, MSSQL, MongoDB);
- to implement best practices for security, performance, and maintainability;
- to conduct code reviews, enforce coding standards, and drive technical improvements;
- toead Agile ceremonies (sprint planning, stand-ups, retrospectives) and ensure smooth collaboration across teams.

Please note:
For our customers, knowledge of English is extremely important;
It is a contractor position, no employee benefits will be included in the contract.

We are looking for consultant experienced in Electron.js to assist in configuring and troubleshooting Electron work environment around Electron Builder, TypeScript and React, assisting developers using windows for development.
Should also be able to setup an automated CI/CD for building (target: windows first, then macos and linux), signing, and upgrading the application.
All setup must be able to be executed in linux-based docker containers.
The scope for this initial engagement is:
* start with a company-specific skeleton project;
* create bash script to generate windows executable using linux docker containers;
* sign the windows executable file (self-signed cert is ok for now);
* automate upload to S3 compatible storage (https access to bucket already provided);
* configure app to implement automated update checks and automated updates;
The project will be provided as github private repo, and CI/CD must be executable there but not using the github actions (as the final CI/CD is likely not going to be github). 
All code to be submitted to the github project (modifications to project, automation scripts, relevant documentation).
